      "penalty": 0.33,
      "category": "Regular Expressions",
      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | Regular Expressions</strong></div>\n<p>Which of the following regular expressions represents the language of all binary strings over $\\{0, 1\\}$ where every 0 is immediately followed by at least two 1s?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    Any sequence of 1s can appear anywhere ($(1)^*$). When a 0 appears, it must be followed by at least two 1s, which can be followed by any number of additional 1s ($011 1^*$). Kleene star of $(1 + 0111^*)^*$ or $(1 + 0111^*)^*$ covers all valid strings including $\\epsilon$.\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "html": "<span>$(1 + 011)^* $</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$(1 + 011)^* $</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "html": "<span>$(1^* 011)^* $</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$(1^* 011)^* $</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "html": "<span>$(1 + 0111^*)^* $</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$(1 + 0111^*)^* $</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "html": "<span>$1^* (011 1^*)^* $</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$1^* (011 1^*)^* $</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "discussUrl": "https://gateoverflow.in"
    },
    {
