      "category": "DFA Minimization",
      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | DFA Minimization</strong></div>\n<p>What is the minimum number of states in a DFA accepting the set of all binary strings over $\\{0, 1\\}$ ending with the substring `101`?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    To recognize a string ending with a specific pattern of length $k$, a minimal DFA requires $k+1$ states for the prefixes $\\{\\epsilon, 1, 10, 101\\}$. Here $k = 3 \\implies 3 + 1 = 4$ states.\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "options": [],
      "correctAnswer": "4",
      "discussUrl": "https://gateoverflow.in"
    },
