      "category": "Grammars and Ambiguity",
      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | Grammars and Ambiguity</strong></div>\n<p>Which of the following Context-Free Grammars is/are <strong>AMBIGUOUS</strong>?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <b>A:</b> String $aaa$ has two distinct leftmost derivations ($S(SS) \\to a(SS) \\to a(aa)$ vs $(SS)S$).<br/><b>B:</b> Generates $a^n b^n$ with unique derivation (unambiguous).<br/><b>C:</b> $\\epsilon$ can be derived via $A$ or $B$ (two derivation trees).<br/><b>D:</b> Classic ambiguous arithmetic grammar ($id + id \\times id$).\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "html": "<span>$S \\to SS \\mid a$</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$S \\to SS \\mid a$</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "html": "<span>$S \\to aSb \\mid \\epsilon$</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$S \\to aSb \\mid \\epsilon$</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "html": "<span>$S \\to A \\mid B, \\; A \\to aAb \\mid \\epsilon, \\; B \\to aBb \\mid \\epsilon$</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$S \\to A \\mid B, \\; A \\to aAb \\mid \\epsilon, \\; B \\to aBb \\mid \\epsilon$</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "html": "<span>$E \\to E + E \\mid E \\times E \\mid id$</span>",
          "textHtml": "<span>$E \\to E + E \\mid E \\times E \\mid id$</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A;C;D",
      "discussUrl": "https://gateoverflow.in"
    },
