      "category": "Chomsky Normal Form",
      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | Chomsky Normal Form</strong></div>\n<p>In Chomsky Normal Form (CNF), if a string $w$ of length $|w| = 15$ is derived from the start symbol, what is the exact number of derivation steps used?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    In CNF, every production is of the form $A \\to BC$ or $A \\to a$. Deriving a string of length $n$ requires exactly $n-1$ binary rule applications ($A \\to BC$) followed by $n$ terminal rule applications ($A \\to a$). Total steps $= (n - 1) + n = 2n - 1 = 2(15) - 1 = 29$.\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "options": [],
      "correctAnswer": "29",
      "discussUrl": "https://gateoverflow.in"
    },
