      "category": "Pumping Lemma",
      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | Pumping Lemma</strong></div>\n<p>For the regular language $L = (01)^+$, what is the smallest valid pumping length $p$ satisfying the Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    For any string $w \\in L$ with $|w| \\ge 2$, say $w = 01$, we can choose $x = \\epsilon, y = 01, z = \\epsilon$. Then $y = 01$ can be pumped: $x y^i z = (01)^i \\in L$ for all $i \\ge 0$. The minimum pumping length is 2.\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "options": [],
      "correctAnswer": "2",
      "discussUrl": "https://gateoverflow.in"
    },
