      "questionHtml": "<div class=\"res_question_text\">\n<div class=\"q-source-tag\"><strong>⚡ GO Classes CS 2027 Style | Closure Properties</strong></div>\n<p>The family of Context-Free Languages is <strong>NOT</strong> closed under which of the following operations?</p>\n<div class=\"solution-explanation-panel\" style=\"margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);\">\n  <strong style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">💡 Official Solution & Step-by-Step Derivation:</strong>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    Context-Free Languages are closed under Union, Concatenation, Kleene Star, Homomorphism, and Reversal. They are NOT closed under Intersection, Complement, or Set Difference.\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
